===Climate===
[[File:Tokuyama Mackerel Boats.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Mackerel fishing boats returning to Tokuyama harbor at dawn during the autumn run.]]

Tokuyama Prefecture experiences a humid subtropical climate (Köppen classification Cfa) moderated by the warm maritime currents of the Shendan Ocean. Unlike the inland prefectures that experience extreme temperature variations, Tokuyama's coastal position ensures mild winters and warm, humid summers with consistent rainfall throughout the year.

The ocean exerts a powerful moderating influence on the prefecture's climate. Winter temperatures rarely drop below 10°C, even in the coldest months, while summer highs are tempered by persistent sea breezes. The prefecture receives abundant precipitation, particularly during the summer monsoon season when warm, moisture-laden air from the Shendan Ocean produces prolonged periods of rainfall. The autumn months bring the celebrated {{nihongo|mackerel season|鯖の季節|Saba no Kisetsu}}, when cooling ocean temperatures drive massive schools of mackerel into the prefecture's bays—a natural phenomenon that has shaped the region's economy and cuisine for centuries.

As illustrated by the climate data for the capital city below, the region is characterized by warm, stable temperatures year-round with high humidity and significant precipitation. The data highlights the maritime influence, with minimal seasonal temperature variation compared to the inland and highland prefectures.

